{# ── Standard display ad (Google AdSense) — enterprise-grade ─────────────────
   Renders ONLY when a publisher client + ad slot are configured (admin settings
   or ADSENSE_CLIENT / ADSENSE_SLOT env) — otherwise nothing shows, so dev and
   un-monetised deployments stay clean. Labeled "Advertisement", responsive, and
   height-reserved (CSS) to avoid layout shift. The unit is LAZY-loaded (only when
   it nears the viewport) and the whole block COLLAPSES if the network returns no
   ad, so users never see an empty placeholder. The adsbygoogle.js loader + the
   lazy/collapse controller are added once per page by the host template
   (see shop/index.twig). Pass `slot` to target a specific unit; defaults to the
   configured `adsense_slot`. #}
{% set _adslot = slot|default(adsense_slot) %}
{% if adsense_client and _adslot %}
<aside class="ad-slot" role="complementary" aria-label="Advertisement" data-ad-lazy>
  <span class="ad-slot__label">Advertisement</span>
  <ins class="adsbygoogle"
       style="display:block"
       data-ad-client="{{ adsense_client }}"
       data-ad-slot="{{ _adslot }}"
       data-ad-format="auto"
       data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins>
</aside>
{% endif %}
